		Bestiary: {
			TinCan: A tin can. It is full of explosives. Nobody knows who filled it.
			GlueSlime: A slime made of glue. It does not bite. It does not need to. Everything it touches becomes part of a growing, screaming pile.
			SlipperyFrog: Slides sideways forever. When something gets in its way it simply is somewhere else. Scientists are baffled.
			ZombieSalesman: Rose from the grave to hit his quota. While he's around, every item icon in your inventory is a zombie. That's his pitch.
			ZombieIntern: Sits around and does nothing. Technically part of the invasion. Nobody has told it what to do.
			ZombieCEO: Tanky, loud, obnoxious, and gets stronger for every zombie on screen. Has never written a line of code.
			HoppingLavaBucket: Someone filled a bucket with lava and it got ideas. Hops around aimlessly, burns on contact.
			DrippyWaterBucket: A water bucket with ambition. Hops around, leaves everything damp.
			BouncingHoneyBucket: A honey bucket that heals you a little and makes you sticky. The nicest enemy in the game.
			ChaoticShimmerBucket: A bottomless shimmer bucket on the move. Anything it bumps into gets shimmered.
			DualFlintlockPistols: Two pistols, no owner, plenty of ammunition. They take turns.
			BiomePile: A heap of whatever makes the biome you're standing in. Break it for fishing loot.
			CommaDotComma: Three pixels. Mortal only between 3:21 and 3:24 AM on a full moon. Do not kill it. Seriously.
			GlueBat: A slightly faster cave bat, white, and sticky.
			GlueDigger: A slightly faster digger, white, and sticky.
			MoreZombies: A very large zombie that makes more zombies every time you hit it. Blood moons only.
			SpinningWorm: Falls out of the rain, spinning. Dies on impact and leaves a worm. The rain is weird here.
			ScreamingFlinx: Falls out of blizzards, screaming the whole way down. The scream hurts.
			Doppleganger: Appears next to town NPCs at night wearing your name and your clothes. If you hit it, it leaves.
			Gremlot: Sells ten random items from the other shops in town at half price. Restocks at midnight. Always called Gremlot.
			RatMerchant: Sells the last twenty things you threw in the trash, one gold each. Moves in once you've trashed twenty different things.
			ChaoticBeholder: Sells everything with "Chaos" in the name once the Chaotic Slime is dead. Talking to him is a one in twenty gamble.
			Shlue: Two glue slimes in a trench coat, with googly eyes. Moves in after fifty glue creatures have died. Always called Shlue.
			ChaoticSlime: A King Slime that can't settle on a colour and keeps teleporting. Beat it to unlock the Chaotic Beholder.
			SlotBarCaterpillar: Steals your bottom inventory row and wears it as a body. Wiggles. Throws your stuff at you. 10,000 HP of pure inconvenience.
			BonemassOfSkeletron: One time in four the Old Man's curse summons this instead. A slow heap of bones that spews bones, sweeps hands, rains bones and raises skeletons. Legally Skeletron.
		}

		Events: {
			DeliriumName: Delirium
			InvasionName: Corporate Zombies
			InvasionDawn: Dawn breaks. The corporate zombies have clocked out.
			DeliriumStart: Silhouettes gather at the edge of your vision...
			DeliriumEnd: The silhouettes fade. Was any of that real?
			InvasionStart: The Corporate Zombie Invasion has begun! Check your inbox.
			InvasionProgress: The corporate zombies are being downsized...
			InvasionCEO: The Zombie CEO has left his office!
			InvasionEnd: The Corporate Zombie Invasion has been defeated! The company has been dissolved.
			CEODown: The Zombie CEO has been given a golden parachute (into the ground).
			MoonShoesStart: Tonight is the Night of Moon Shoes! Everything is floaty.
			MoonShoesEnd: The Moon Shoes come off. Gravity resumes.
			Beacon0: A beacon makes it rain.
			Beacon1: A beacon summons a storm.
			Beacon2: A beacon calls the blizzard winds.
			Beacon3: A beacon banishes the clouds.
			Beacon4: A beacon whips up a sandstorm.
			Beacon5: A beacon fills the air with jelly. Everything bounces.
			Beacon6: A beacon makes it rain frogs. Watch your step.
			BeaconRemoved: The weather beacon is gone. The weather is weather again.
			BonemassRises: The curse takes a different shape... the Bonemass of Skeletron rises!
			ChaoticSlimeDown: The Chaotic Slime has been defeated! A Chaotic Beholder will want a house.
		}

		Dehydrator.NotEligible: The Dehydrator only accepts living things that contain water (critters, fish, plants).

